From d995acf3a4f5333ce60ed56494af5c5235f8ac08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicole@muzz.in>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 19:07:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] layout: size table cells' replaced and scrollable children
 like Blink

Replaced children of a cell resolve percentage block sizes against the
cell's fixed block size while the columns are sized too, so an auto-width
table holding img{height:100%} in a 100px cell is as wide as the scaled
image (77.7px) rather than its natural width. While rows are measured, a
restricted cell (fixed block size, or a table whose height is not auto)
lays out its in-flow block-level children that scroll in the block axis
and have a percentage block size as if that percentage resolved against
zero, so their overflow no longer grows the row.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
